---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import DocsTopBar from '../components/DocsTopBar.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Support, Glyph"
  description="Answers to the things that come up most with Glyph. If yours isn't here, email me."
>
  <DocsTopBar />
  <main class="support">
    <header class="head">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Answers to what comes up most. If yours isn't here, email
        <a href="mailto:contact@glyph.moe">contact@glyph.moe</a>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="qa">
      <div class="qa-list">
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>How do I add a novel source?</h3>
          <p>
            Glyph doesn't ship with any sources. Go to Settings → Extensions → tap <strong>+</strong
            >, paste a repository URL (shared by the community), tap <strong>Fetch</strong>, then
            <strong>Install</strong>. Installed sources show up in the Browse tab.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>An extension won't load or won't fetch anything.</h3>
          <p>
            Go to Settings → Extensions → tap the repository → <strong>Refresh</strong> the source. If
            that doesn't help, Settings → Storage → <strong>Clear Extension Cache</strong>, then
            reopen the app.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>A chapter says "Could not load chapter".</h3>
          <p>
            Usually the novel site is down or blocking requests, or your connection dropped. Tap
            <strong>Retry</strong>. If it keeps happening, check whether the extension has an update
            in Settings → Extensions.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>The reader shows a white screen or loads forever.</h3>
          <p>
            Go back and reopen the chapter. If it's still stuck, Settings → Storage →
            <strong>Clear Extension Cache</strong>, then try again, the extension may need to
            refetch the content.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>Can I read offline?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. On a novel's detail page, tap the download icon to save chapters, or all of them.
            Downloads live on your device and read without a connection. The Downloads section in
            your Library shows what's saved and how much storage it uses.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>Does Glyph track me?</h3>
          <p>
            No. No analytics, no accounts, no tracking. Your library and reading progress stay on
            your device, syncing only through your own iCloud if you're signed in. Extensions run
            sandboxed and can only reach their declared site.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>My reading progress didn't appear on a new device.</h3>
          <p>
            Progress syncs through iCloud. Make sure you're signed into the same Apple ID and that
            iCloud Drive is enabled for Glyph (Settings → iCloud), then give it a few minutes to
            sync.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="qa-item">
          <h3>How do I delete my data?</h3>
          <p>
            Everything is stored locally on your device. Remove novels one by one, or in Settings →
            Storage clear reading history, downloads, or the extension cache. Deleting the app
            removes all of it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="qa-more">
        More in the <a href="/docs/faq">full FAQ</a> and the
        <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bug">
      <h2>Reporting a bug</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:contact@glyph.moe">contact@glyph.moe</a> with as much of this as you can:
      </p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><Icon name="check" size={15} /> <span>iOS version and device model</span></li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={15} /> <span>Glyph version (Settings → About)</span></li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={15} /> <span>Steps to reproduce</span></li>
        <li>
          <Icon name="check" size={15} />
          <span>What you expected vs. what actually happened</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <Icon name="check" size={15} />
          <span>A diagnostic report (Settings → Share Diagnostic Report), if relevant</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="bug-note">
        Diagnostic reports never leave your device unless you share them. They carry app logs and
        network history, no personal data. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="security">
      <span class="security-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="shield" size={18} /></span>
      <h2>Security disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Found a vulnerability in the app, the SDK, the CLI, or an official extension? Email
        <a href="mailto:contact@glyph.moe">contact@glyph.moe</a> directly rather than opening a public
        issue. I'll acknowledge within 72 hours.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .support {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 140px 24px 96px;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .head {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(38px, 5.5vw, 48px);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-variation-settings:
      'SOFT' 30,
      'opsz' 144;
  }
  .intro {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .intro a {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* Common questions */
  .qa {
    margin-bottom: 64px;
  }
  .qa-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .qa-item {
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .qa-item:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .qa-item h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .qa-item p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .qa-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .qa-more {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .qa-more a {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* Bug report */
  .bug {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .bug h2,
  .security h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 22px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .bug p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .bug p a {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 11px;
  }
  .checklist li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 11px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .checklist li :global(svg) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .bug-note {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .bug-note a {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* Security */
  .security {
    padding: 24px 26px;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-dim) 55%, var(--bg-surface));
  }
  .security-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 38px;
    height: 38px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 14%, transparent);
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .security h2 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .security p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .security a {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .support {
      padding: 100px 16px 64px;
    }
    .head h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
    }
    .security {
      padding: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
